INT. DEEP-SEA HABITAT, COMMON ROOM - SHIFT CHANGE

A cramped steel cylinder with a single porthole of black water. Bunks fold from the walls. A coffee machine gurgles. Condensation drips from the pipes in a slow, steady count.

Six crew members cluster around a fold-out table playing a card game no one is winning.

COMMANDER ASTRID LINDQVIST-OKOYE (50s) deals. TECHNICIAN BENEDICT ARCHAMBAULT-LI (30s) fans his cards. DR. SOLEDAD VARGAS-EZEKIEL (40s) frowns at her hand. COOK RAMONA "MONA" ABARCA-NIELSEN (30s) pours coffee. ENGINEER THADDEUS MWANGI-PELLETIER (60s) hums off-key. And the youngest, SPECIALIST KAMALA DEVI-BRANDT (20s), stares at the porthole.

ASTRID
(to the table)
Antes in.

BENEDICT
I fold.

SOLEDAD
You haven't seen the cards.

BENEDICT
I've seen your face.

MONA
(over them)
Coffee's up, who wants some?

THADDEUS
Me.

KAMALA
Not me.

SOLEDAD
Mona, put two sugars in mine, would you, and Benedict --

BENEDICT
Don't tell me what to do with my own hand --

ASTRID
Everyone, quiet.

They stop. The pipes drip. Kamala is still looking at the porthole.

ASTRID (CONT'D)
(to Kamala)
What is it?

KAMALA
(without turning)
Nothing.

THADDEUS
(muttering)
There's always something.

MONA
Don't start, Thad.

THADDEUS
I'm just saying --

SOLEDAD
(over him)
He's right, though. The pressure gauge ticked.

BENEDICT
It ticks all the time.

SOLEDAD
Not like that.

MONA
(setting down the pot)
Like what?

ASTRID
Like a heartbeat.

Everyone looks at her. She lays down her cards, face up.

ASTRID (CONT'D)
(to herself)
I knew I'd heard it before.

A long, low note rolls through the hull. The coffee ripples in the cups. Nobody moves. Nobody speaks. Then Kamala turns from the porthole and smiles.

KAMALA
It's only the whales.
